From: Claudius <claudiusthebot@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] S9: the night run changes (exit and kill log, async GPU submits, prewarm, kqworkloop limits, panel brightness, 60 Hz timer)

The kernel changes of the perf2 and night runs (docs/ios27/NIGHT.md), every one behind a bit of the boot-arg
sweetspeed=<mask> (default 0: nothing changes; the bits are listed in xnu/files-12377/osfmk/arm64/sweet_a64e.c):
  32    exit and kill log, SIGKILL backtrace, spawn limits log   (kern_exit.c, kern_sig.c, kern_exec.c, task.c)
  64    asynchronous GPU submits (StarbiteMali 0x105/0x106, starlte_gpu.c) and HakiosWaitsForGPU
  128   page-cache prewarm of the GL stack and the UI daemons    (bsd_init.c)
  256   ignore launchd's kqworkloop limits at spawn              (kern_exec.c)
  512   the S6E3HA8 panel (bsd/dev/hakios.s6e3ha8.c, patch 0428), iOS 27 swap brightness, brightness setProperties
  1024  an absolute 60 Hz deadline for the framebuffer timer      (SweetFramebuffer.cpp)
  2048  CoreAnimation pacing aids (sweetfb_cav)                   (SweetFramebuffer.cpp)
  4096  scripted frame-rate input, 8192 scripted brightness-slider input   (starlte_touch.c)
